/target
/.ci-artifacts/
/.cargo-home
**/*.rs.bk
*.iso
*.img
*.bin
# OT-27a (2026-06-21): vendor device-firmware blobs are NO LONGER committed.
# The MT7601U firmware (`kernel/assets/firmware/mediatek/mt7601u.bin`) is staged
# onto the boot image as a Limine module by xtask and looked up at runtime — the
# same out-of-band, not-in-git discipline as the AI model blob (binary +
# licensing). It stays on disk locally; `*.bin` above keeps it untracked. See
# ADR-054 (amended) + the firmware_blob() loader in the mt7601u driver.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Scratch artifacts — boot logs, build outputs, ad-hoc text capture at repo root.
# Kept on disk for local reference; not committed.
boot-log-*.txt
baseline-build.txt
build-*.txt

# BUILD-5b operator staging folder — local working copy of files for the
# OptiPlex 7080 Micro hardware session. Reproducible from `target/` outputs +
# the Plans/ execution guide; not a canonical source.
/BUILD-5b-staging/

# Tool config directories for AI coders / IDE assistants
.qwen/
.claude/

# Accidental capture from agent processes that did not expand $HOME correctly.
# Contains Claude Code PAI memory state belonging to the user account, not the repo.
${HOME}/

# Local operational tooling (Jira dispatch) and its bytecode cache.
# Referenced by CLAUDE.md; kept on disk, not committed.
jira-dispatcher.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Living website
/website/

# Per-seat coder worktrees (PL standing ops, 2026-07-20). Each CLI coder gets its
# own persistent git worktree under Workers/<seat> so two seats never share one
# physical tree (the recurring shared-tree collision / cross-push hazard). These
# are separate worktrees of THIS repo, nested inside the main tree's working dir,
# so they must be ignored here to keep `git status` clean. See
# docs/runbook-per-seat-worktrees.md.
/Workers/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/
